    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0342" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2303</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania, Servia, and Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-10T14:00:00+01:44">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 10, 1915, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 12, 7.50 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>197. Political information. Definite arrangements have been concluded between the
                    Austro-German and Roumanian Governments, for the purchase by the former of fifty
                    thousand wagons of Roumanian wheat, only minor details remaining to be
                    adjusted.</p>
                <p>It is now evident that Roumania will take no action before spring as to
                    participation in the war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
